{
  "id": "ss.relic.tithe",
  "name": "Tithe",
  "description": "A shallow wooden bowl with a chitin lip, seen from a little above, holding blood to two-thirds: the level sits well below the rim, a dark-red tide mark on the inner wall shows where it used to stand, and the band of dry wall between the two is the third that is gone. One drop hangs in the air above the bowl with a bead below it, lifted out rather than falling in. The relic takes thirty from the health bar and gives thirty to the hit, and a measure taken out of a vessel is the trade drawn as an object. The inside of the bowl is red and not dark, so the ring of the lip does not read as the rim of a hole.",
